{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"FreedomTerminal.Koegaki","latestVersion":"1.15.5","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.a118da44.png","priority":1,"sha256":"a118da44e8a863b95b6dabc8da71768a874462e481a15de18e8f95979c8d5b07","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright Vishut Dhar","description":"Private push-to-talk dictation that runs entirely on your machine.","license":"Proprietary","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright Vishut Dhar","description":"Private push-to-talk dictation that runs entirely on your machine.","license":"Proprietary","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Koegaki is push-to-talk dictation for Windows. Hold a key, speak, and your words appear wherever you are typing. The speech model runs entirely on-device, so audio and text never leave your machine. No account, no cloud, no subscription. 30-day free trial, then a one-time purchase covers Mac and Windows.","moniker":"koegaki","name":"Koegaki","packageUrl":"https://koegaki.com","privacyUrl":"https://koegaki.com/privacy","publisher":"Freedom Terminal","publisherUrl":"https://freedom-terminal.com","releaseNotes":"- With Tap to start and stop, long speech with no pause is no longer cut in the middle of a word. Koegaki used to split it after 14 seconds wherever that fell, which could change a word or drop one at the split. It now waits for a pause. Speech that runs past 20 seconds with none is split at its quietest moment.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/vishutdhar/koegaki-releases/releases/tag/v1.15.5","tags":["dictation","speech-to-text","voice-typing","offline","privacy"]}},"longDescription":"Koegaki is push-to-talk dictation for Windows. Hold a key, speak, and your words appear wherever you are typing. The speech model runs entirely on-device, so audio and text never leave your machine. No account, no cloud, no subscription. 30-day free trial, then a one-time purchase covers Mac and Windows.","moniker":"koegaki","name":"Koegaki","packageUrl":"https://koegaki.com","privacyUrl":"https://koegaki.com/privacy","publisher":"Freedom Terminal","publisherUrl":"https://freedom-terminal.com","releaseNotes":"- With Tap to start and stop, long speech with no pause is no longer cut in the middle of a word. Koegaki used to split it after 14 seconds wherever that fell, which could change a word or drop one at the split. It now waits for a pause. Speech that runs past 20 seconds with none is split at its quietest moment.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/vishutdhar/koegaki-releases/releases/tag/v1.15.5","tags":["dictation","speech-to-text","voice-typing","offline","privacy"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.15.5/app.json","detailSha256":"3e7018f0fffde18aa276c3f62f9b71d72ffbf60fe89f86f61b3df3a9d1cd6d32","releaseDate":"2026-11-11","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.15.5"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.15.4/app.json","detailSha256":"95785d1be62f17558c9af397ac5f9ec9787ea032db3619d1b62973c68c468efe","releaseDate":"2026-11-10","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.15.4"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.15.3/app.json","detailSha256":"27d10f42289ea7360237ad0db13eafd01657ab97de5b717b2ab57eefdaa0ff12","releaseDate":"2026-10-29","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.15.3"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.15.2/app.json","detailSha256":"c6c27d94605ffd47807de1f08ff646c05a5333e68c00286d5c54ed5a998b706c","releaseDate":"2026-10-20","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.15.2"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.15.0/app.json","detailSha256":"ba37f677d2e55d32689330127ff50cb1dcf6a12fff4f396da63de4d4b59dc907","releaseDate":"2026-10-17","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.15.0"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.14.1/app.json","detailSha256":"9fb1bcb7f216e1a6682684d1c561d1233666d0f4bc0f62ebc179ff481ac2c06b","releaseDate":